<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Schönbrunn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Schönbrunn · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-fifth-coalition">War of the Fifth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Schönbrunn was signed at Schönbrunn Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> on 14 October 1809, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-fifth-coalition">War of the Fifth Coalition</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Austria ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-galicia">West Galicia</a> to the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a> and other lands to France, which formed them into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyrian-provinces">Illyrian Provinces</a>. Austria lost several million subjects and its access to the sea and paid a heavy indemnity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-schonbrunn.jpg" alt="Treaty of Schönbrunn" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Monnet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trait%C3%A9_de_paix_conclu_%C3%A0_Vienne_le_14_octobre_1809.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
